American is the latest climber to die on  Mount Everest Colorado attorney Chris  kulish collapsed on his way down after  reaching the summit he is at least the  11th fatality there this season CTM  national correspondent jury kanou-kun is  here with more on that story so Jericka  what do the experienced climbers say now  about conditions on that mountain well  they say that it's really difficult no  matter how ready you are for this trip  we spoke to someone on the same  expedition as Chris Coolidge who says  the climber was fully prepared for his  own mission to scale the world's tallest  mountain but he was not prepared for  what he saw when he got there too many  people dangerously vying for the same  experience it's the top of the world but  on an icy platform no wider than two  ping pong tables that over 29,000 feet  capturing the moment can get dangerous  that's what made it scary for me is that  there was a large group on the summit at  the time I got there there was a  subgroup that was very rude and unruly  and was basically pushing so that they  could get better pictures of themselves  and I just thought this is not safe but  before you even make it to the top  traffic jams on the final few feet an  area known as the Death Zone at that  altitude there is not enough oxygen for  humans to breathe so vital supplies are  used up while the primers just wait too  many are navigating to smaller space and  dr. doreen says too many of them don't  know what they're doing I was surprised  at how many people were you know above  26,000 feet and had really were  obviously we're either not fit or not  experienced and probably shouldn't have  been there during witnessed firsthand  the deadly combination and I certainly  wasn't prepared to pass dead bodies that  were attached to the safety line it was  very difficult  on May 29th 1953 when Sir Edmund Hillary  became the first climber to reach the  summit its Sherpa Tenzing Norgay it was  global news 66 years almost to the day  scaling the world's tallest mountain has  become an Instagram moment a feat not  just for the best but for almost anyone  with a bucket list and we should add  that dr. doreen told us that despite all  the well-documented problems on the  mountain he does not think that Chris  Coolidge died as a result of the  overcrowding nor was he inexperienced  coolish was extremely fit even at 62 and  was climbing with what he described as  probably the best guide team on the  mountain Anthony still can't get over  the pictures of that line up there  Jericka amazing thank you
 

